Theorem~\ref{thm:detection-lb-informal} shows that detection performance improves when the distribution of $\Delta=f(x,s)-f(x',s')$ have heavier tails, where both $f(x,s),f(x',s')\sim P_F$.  We analyze several choices of heavy-tailed  $P_F$ for maximizing $\int_{1-\lambda}^1Q(u)du$ (see details in Appendix \ref{apdx:tails}).
