\section{Conclusion}
In this work, we present \sysname, a novel LLM framework for Verilog code generation. We introduce a hallucination taxonomy, including symbolic, knowledge and logical hallucinations. \sysname addresses these challenges through a three-stage methodology focused on reducing hallucinations in LLM-generated code while enhancing adherence to the practices of HDL engineers. Experimental results demonstrate that \sysname outperforms existing state-of-the-art methods and that our three techniques are effective individually. 

