\subsection{Test-Time Scaling Techniques}

HRET incorporates advanced test-time scaling techniques to enhance evaluation quality through multiple inference strategies. These methods are particularly valuable for Korean language evaluation, where single predictions may not fully capture model capabilities due to linguistic complexity and cultural contexts.

The framework supports three primary approaches: \textbf{Best-of-N Sampling}, \textbf{Self-Consistency} with majority voting, and \textbf{Beam Search} for optimal decoding paths. These techniques can be combined with various evaluation methods, including LLM-as-a-judge assessments.

Table~\ref{tab:test-time-scaling} demonstrates test-time scaling effectiveness on HAERAE Reasoning Challenge (HRC), evaluating Korean reasoning across science, mathematics, and quiz domains.

