\section{Usage Examples and Tutorials}
\label{sec:usage-examples}

This section provides advanced examples and tutorials for using HRET beyond the basic functionality introduced in the main paper.

\subsection{Advanced Backend Usage}

HRET supports multiple backend integrations beyond standard HuggingFace models:

\subsubsection{LiteLLM and OpenAI-Compatible APIs}

Access over 30 LLM providers and self-hosted servers:

\begin{lstlisting}[language=python]
# Using LiteLLM for cloud-based models
results = evaluator.run(
    model="litellm",
    model_params={
        "model_name": "gpt-4",
        "api_key": "your-api-key-here",
    },
    dataset="haerae_bench",
    evaluation_method="string_match"
)

# Using OpenAI-compatible endpoints for self-hosted models
results = evaluator.run(
    model="openai",
    model_params={
        "model_name": "local-llama-2-13b",
        "api_base": "http://localhost:8000/v1",
    },
    dataset="haerae_bench",
    evaluation_method="string_match"
)
\end{lstlisting}

\subsection{Evaluation Methods}

\subsubsection{String Match and Log Probability Evaluation}

HRET offers flexible text matching with various normalization options:

\begin{lstlisting}[language=python]
# String matching with normalization options
results = evaluator.run(
    model="huggingface",
    model_params={"model_name_or_path":"Qwen/Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct"},
    dataset="haerae_bench",
    evaluation_method='string_match',
    evaluator_params={
        "ignore_case": True,
        "ignore_punctuation": True,
        "extract_answer": True,
    }
)

# Log probability evaluation for MCQA
results = evaluator.run(
    model="huggingface",
    dataset="haerae_bench",
    evaluation_method='log_likelihood',
    dataset_params={"base_prompt_template": "{query} ### Answer:"},
)
\end{lstlisting}


These examples demonstrate HRET's capabilities for Korean language model evaluation beyond the basic functionality presented in the main paper. The project repository provides comprehensive tutorials and documentation in both Korean and English, including additional examples, best practices, and implementation guidelines.


\section{Real-World Usage}
\label{appendix:real-world-usage}

Beyond academic evaluation frameworks, HRET has been adopted in production environments across the Korean NLP industry. Authors' affiliated organizations, including Shinhan Securities and OneLineAI, have integrated HRET into their model validation and post-training evaluation workflows, demonstrating the framework's practical utility in real-world deployment scenarios. Additionally, the Haerae Reasoning Challenge (HRC) officially employs HRET to score all participant submissions under standardized protocols, ensuring fairness and transparency in competitive evaluations.
This production adoption validates HRET's reliability and effectiveness beyond controlled research settings, confirming its value for industry practitioners requiring robust evaluation infrastructure.

\section*{Ethics Statement}

latexHRET aims to improve reproducibility and fairness in Korean LLM evaluation. However, we acknowledge several ethical considerations: (1) standardized evaluation frameworks may inadvertently favor certain model architectures or training approaches; (2) benchmark selection reflects our research perspectives and may not capture all aspects of Korean language competency; (3) language consistency enforcement, while promoting Korean language assessment, may disadvantage multilingual models in certain contexts. We encourage the community to contribute diverse benchmarks and evaluation methods to ensure broad representation of Korean language capabilities. All integrated datasets respect original licensing and guidelines.




