%
% RECONSTRUCT()
%
\noindent\textbf{reconstruct}(y, n\_comp=3, options=None, return\_error=False)

Performs inverse transformation followed by its expansion to $\mathbf{X}$ space. \textbf{reconstruct(y)} $\equiv$ \textbf{expand(inverse(y))}.

\textbf{Parameters}:

\quad Same as for \textbf{inverse()}.

\textbf{Returns}:

