% Voiced Electromyography(EMG)-to-Speech (V-ETS) models reconstruct speech from muscle activity signals, supporting studies of phoneme production and articulation development thus offering insights into how speech units relate to muscle activity—relevant for interdisciplinary research.
% Voiced Electromyography(EMG)-to-Speech (V-ETS) models reconstruct speech from muscle activity signals, facilitating applications such as neurolaryngologic diagnostics.
