\subsubsection{Results}

We used text descriptions as control conditions for the noise prediction network, intervening with inverted latents during the sampling process at regular intervals of 10 timesteps, starting from \(t=0\). When intervention occurs near the end of sampling, the sound is almost indistinguishable from the original sound, and the reference sound components are difficult to recognize. We therefore intervened with latent representations in the middle-to-late stages of the sampling process to achieve optimal fusion results. Figure \ref{fig:sound_set} shows fusion examples.

