where the last step required $2k\gamma/2 \geq 1/2$, which is true in case $k\geq 2, \gamma>1/2$. It is not hard to see that $\frac{1}{\ell!2^{t+\ell}p^3} \leq 1$, so that the final query complexity becomes $\frac{m^2 \epsilon}{1-\gamma}$.
