Theorem~\ref{thm:incomplete_lower_bound} motivates the study of adaptive algorithms. Ideally, we would have more precise non-asymptotic results, especially because the upper bound of Algorithm~\ref{alg:LS-incomplete-queries} contains large constants. Or otherwise, it might be possible to extend this result for a larger exponent of $m$ (as done in \cite{halpern_representation_2023}), by adapting the instance. Moreover, obviously, a lower bound for adaptive setting is desirable. Both are left for future work.

