\begin{equation}
\underset{y}{\mathop{\inf }}\,\left( \underset{j\in M}{\mathop{\max }}\,{{y}_{j}}-\sum\limits_{j\in M}{{{\lambda }_{j}}{{y}_{j}}} \right)
\label{eq42}
\end{equation}
(a) If $\lambda \ge 0\ {{1}^{T}}\lambda =1$, then $\sum\limits_{j\in M}{{{\lambda }_{j}}{{y}_{j}}}\le \sum\limits_{j\in M}{{{\lambda }_{j}}\underset{j}{\mathop{\max }}\,{{y}_{j}}=\underset{j}{\mathop{\max }}\,{{y}_{j}}}$ with equality if $y=0$, so in that case:
