\end{itemize}

This shift, known as the \textbf{"FAISS Hybrid Paradox"}, suggests that \textbf{BGE-Large}'s embeddings are better suited for \textbf{initial retrieval} but are \textbf{less compatible} with \textbf{LLM-based relevance assessments}. In contrast, \textbf{MiniLM-v6} benefits significantly from \textbf{LLM reranking}, showing a \textbf{significant performance gain} post-reranking. This indicates that \textbf{MiniLM-v6}'s embeddings align better with how \textbf{GPT-4o} evaluates relevance in \textbf{retrieval-augmented systems}.

