\begin{abstract}
Hardware acceleration of algorithms is an effective method for improving performance in high-demand computational tasks. 
%
However, developing hardware designs for such acceleration fundamentally differs from software development, as it requires a deep understanding of the highly parallel nature of the hardware architecture. 
%
In this paper, we present a framework for the static analysis of communication within datapath architectures designed for field-programmable gate arrays (FPGAs). 
%
Our framework aims to enhance hardware design and optimization by providing insights into communication patterns within the architecture, which are essential for ensuring efficient data handling. 


