\begin{abstract}
This paper extends \texttt{InfTDA}, a mechanism proposed in (Boninsegna, Silvestri, PETS 2025) for mobility datasets with origin and destination trips, in a general setting. The algorithm presented in this paper works for any dataset of $d$ categorical features and produces a differentially private \emph{synthetic} dataset that answers all \emph{hierarchical} queries, a special case of \emph{marginals}, each with bounded maximum absolute error. 
The algorithm builds upon the TopDown mechanism developed for the 2020 US Census.
\end{abstract}
